1
00:00:03,427 --> 00:00:06,847
[Taiki sighs]
<i>Why does Kyo gotta say weird stuff?</i>

2
00:00:07,723 --> 00:00:09,391
<i>The one I have a crush on is Chinatsu--</i>

3
00:00:09,474 --> 00:00:10,642
[groans, spits coffee]

4
00:00:10,726 --> 00:00:12,144
{\an8}[coughs]

5
00:00:12,227 --> 00:00:15,272
{\an8}Chinatsu, what are you doing here?
You're in my house?

6
00:00:16,773 --> 00:00:19,026
My grandpa's doing well after his surgery.

7
00:00:19,109 --> 00:00:21,570
So I'll be staying here again
starting tomorrow.

8
00:00:21,653 --> 00:00:23,030
I came to bring some stuff.

9
00:00:23,113 --> 00:00:25,532
[Taiki] <i>I guess I knew
she was coming back soon.</i>

10
00:00:25,615 --> 00:00:27,784
Thanks again for taking me in, Taiki.

11
00:00:27,868 --> 00:00:29,536
Uh, you're welcome.

12
00:00:30,162 --> 00:00:32,539
But tonight,
I'll be sleeping over at Karen's.

13
00:00:33,248 --> 00:00:34,541
You two are close.

14
00:00:35,125 --> 00:00:37,544
Well, we have known each other
since kindergarten.

15
00:00:37,627 --> 00:00:39,713
[Taiki] <i>She's acting totally normal.</i>

16
00:00:39,796 --> 00:00:42,549
<i>Was she completely unfazed
by what happened during the play?</i>

17
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:51,558
<i>Or maybe she didn't actually come see it.</i>

18
00:00:52,392 --> 00:00:56,855
<i>But if that were true, she probably
would've told me she couldn't make it.</i>

19
00:00:57,439 --> 00:00:58,356
{\an8}[grunts]

20
00:00:58,440 --> 00:00:59,357
[grunts]

21
00:00:59,441 --> 00:01:00,358
[door opens]

22
00:01:01,026 --> 00:01:03,361
[groans] What a fiasco.

23
00:01:04,029 --> 00:01:06,990
On our way back from shopping,
we were eating popcorn,

24
00:01:07,074 --> 00:01:10,869
and then Chii's mom spilled it
all over the place at our front door.

25
00:01:10,952 --> 00:01:13,997
{\an8}[groans] Trash bags...
where are the trash bags?

26
00:01:14,915 --> 00:01:16,875
Why don't I help you clean it up?

27
00:01:16,958 --> 00:01:18,335
[Yukiko] If you don't mind.

28
00:01:21,838 --> 00:01:23,381
[Taiki] Chinatsu!

29
00:01:24,716 --> 00:01:28,887
Um... about the play
at the Cultural Festival--

30
00:01:33,308 --> 00:01:34,226
[grunts]

31
00:01:37,187 --> 00:01:38,396
[grunts]

32
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:40,232
[laughs]

33
00:01:40,315 --> 00:01:41,399
Aren't those so good?

34
00:01:43,985 --> 00:01:44,903
[grunts]

35
00:01:45,987 --> 00:01:47,656
[Taiki] <i>That is beside the point!</i>

36
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:51,076
<i>I wanted to talk about the rumors.</i>

37
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:54,412
<i>About the kiss,
and if Hina and I are dating...</i>

38
00:01:54,496 --> 00:01:56,289
[gulps]

39
00:01:58,041 --> 00:02:00,377
<i>Even if it isn't bothering Chinatsu...</i>

40
00:02:02,546 --> 00:02:04,589
<i>I still want to talk to her about it.</i>

41
00:02:07,843 --> 00:02:09,845
[opening theme song playing]

42
00:02:34,161 --> 00:02:37,622
BLUE BOX

43
00:03:37,599 --> 00:03:40,560
{\an8}EPISODE 21
A CHANCE TO BLOSSOM

44
00:03:40,644 --> 00:03:42,437
{\an8}[bell chiming]

45
00:03:43,104 --> 00:03:45,440
{\an8}Taiki, I've got your back.

46
00:03:45,523 --> 00:03:46,691
Huh?

47
00:03:47,317 --> 00:03:49,819
[Nishida] Don't you worry.
I know everything.

48
00:03:49,903 --> 00:03:51,613
I know that you didn't kiss Hina,

49
00:03:51,696 --> 00:03:55,200
and that the rumors about you two dating
are a complete lie.

50
00:03:55,825 --> 00:03:57,619
{\an8}The rumors are false, aren't they?

51
00:03:57,702 --> 00:03:59,955
{\an8}[Taiki] Yes, they are,
but could you let up a little?

52
00:04:01,081 --> 00:04:04,542
[crying] Just don't you go
and betray me like Haryu did.

53
00:04:05,418 --> 00:04:09,589
Nishida's secret crush
went to his booth to get her fortune read,

54
00:04:09,673 --> 00:04:13,343
and asked for his help with her crush
on a guy from the track and field club.

55
00:04:13,426 --> 00:04:14,719
Dang.

56
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:16,888
Anyway, I'm relieved.

57
00:04:16,972 --> 00:04:18,723
I'm glad you didn't get hurt.

58
00:04:18,807 --> 00:04:22,477
That was scary when the confetti ball
fell from outta nowhere.

59
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,312
You saw the play, then?

60
00:04:24,396 --> 00:04:26,564
I am your captain after all.

61
00:04:26,648 --> 00:04:30,235
I was there with Haryu, his girlfriend,
and Kano from the girls' basketball team.

62
00:04:30,318 --> 00:04:31,236
[gasps]

63
00:04:32,570 --> 00:04:35,949
[Taiki] <i>What do you know,
I was right. She was there!</i>

64
00:04:37,909 --> 00:04:40,745
Even the second and third-years
are gossiping about it.

65
00:04:40,829 --> 00:04:42,747
[scoffs] Not really a surprise though.

66
00:04:43,581 --> 00:04:45,792
The rhythmic gymnastics girl is famous.

67
00:04:46,668 --> 00:04:48,795
Anyone who was there
knows it was an accident,

68
00:04:48,878 --> 00:04:51,756
but rumors like that
often take on a life of their own.

69
00:04:54,592 --> 00:04:56,511
So make sure you look out for her.

70
00:05:01,599 --> 00:05:02,517
[grunts softly]

71
00:05:03,143 --> 00:05:04,019
[grunts]

72
00:05:05,103 --> 00:05:07,022
The thirst tax, 12,000 yen.

73
00:05:07,105 --> 00:05:09,024
{\an8}Wait, you raised the price again?

74
00:05:09,107 --> 00:05:12,068
No, I didn't.
It's 'cause there's two of you.

75
00:05:12,152 --> 00:05:13,028
Wait, me?

76
00:05:13,737 --> 00:05:15,780
I'm just messing with you!

77
00:05:15,864 --> 00:05:16,781
[girl] Hina!

78
00:05:16,865 --> 00:05:18,408
Mm? Yeah!

79
00:05:20,535 --> 00:05:22,996
On second thought,
she'd never go out with you.

80
00:05:23,079 --> 00:05:24,497
[Taiki groans]

81
00:05:24,581 --> 00:05:26,708
{\an8}If anyone's talking smack about you,

82
00:05:26,791 --> 00:05:28,418
{\an8}I'll smack them right back.

83
00:05:28,501 --> 00:05:30,295
{\an8}Thanks so much, Captain.

84
00:05:32,088 --> 00:05:35,300
[girl] It's them, isn't it?
The ones supposedly dating?

85
00:05:35,967 --> 00:05:38,261
Well, I heard it wasn't true.

86
00:05:38,344 --> 00:05:39,804
Oh. Seriously?

87
00:05:40,764 --> 00:05:42,432
A lot of weird rumors going around.

88
00:05:42,515 --> 00:05:43,600
Are you okay?

89
00:05:43,683 --> 00:05:45,560
You are living with him again, right?

90
00:05:48,146 --> 00:05:49,606
{\an8}[groans]

91
00:05:50,899 --> 00:05:52,692
Did you see that just now?

92
00:05:52,776 --> 00:05:54,319
That was a Steph Curry shot!

93
00:05:56,196 --> 00:05:57,906
[Nagisa] <i>Well,
the point of living with him</i>

94
00:05:57,989 --> 00:06:00,158
<i>is so she can keep playing basketball.</i>

95
00:06:00,241 --> 00:06:01,076
One more.

96
00:06:01,659 --> 00:06:05,246
[Nagisa] <i>I guess Chinatsu just
isn't interested in that kind of gossip.</i>

97
00:06:12,295 --> 00:06:14,589
[Karen] Still,
it's been forever, hasn't it?

98
00:06:15,215 --> 00:06:17,133
You coming to stay over, I mean.

99
00:06:17,217 --> 00:06:19,594
You slept over a lot when we were kids.

100
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:22,597
I've been so tied up with practice lately.

101
00:06:23,389 --> 00:06:25,975
Geez. Everybody's all,
"Practice, practice."

102
00:06:26,059 --> 00:06:27,936
Well, you have your work, too, right?

103
00:06:28,019 --> 00:06:29,604
I mean, I do, but...

104
00:06:30,396 --> 00:06:33,525
Kengo will be busy
with practice for a while,

105
00:06:33,608 --> 00:06:36,027
which means he'll be a little distant.

106
00:06:36,694 --> 00:06:39,322
And I won't hear from him. [sighs]

107
00:06:40,490 --> 00:06:42,784
You say that,
but wouldn't you be mad at him

108
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:44,786
if he prioritized you over his club?

109
00:06:44,869 --> 00:06:46,621
Obviously, I would!

110
00:06:46,704 --> 00:06:49,624
I would never want him
to use me as an excuse.

111
00:06:49,707 --> 00:06:51,376
If I'm being honest,

112
00:06:52,085 --> 00:06:54,796
it's when he's playing badminton
that I hear myself think,

113
00:06:54,879 --> 00:06:56,881
"Gosh, he's just so cool."

114
00:06:59,634 --> 00:07:00,635
{\an8}[Chinatsu sighs]

115
00:07:01,261 --> 00:07:04,139
And that's why,
you'll fill my attention fix!

116
00:07:04,222 --> 00:07:06,641
{\an8}You're lucky to have me. [giggles]

117
00:07:06,724 --> 00:07:09,394
{\an8}I'm cheating on him with you! [giggles]

118
00:07:10,353 --> 00:07:14,274
I really do have to keep pesky bugs
away from you, bestie.

119
00:07:14,357 --> 00:07:15,650
Not bugs.

120
00:07:17,277 --> 00:07:20,405
I'm only bringing this up
'cause they asked me to, okay?

121
00:07:21,114 --> 00:07:23,741
A guy friend of mine
from a different school

122
00:07:23,825 --> 00:07:26,119
asked me to introduce you to him.

123
00:07:26,202 --> 00:07:28,913
He would like to know
if he can get your number.

124
00:07:28,997 --> 00:07:30,290
No, thank you.

125
00:07:30,373 --> 00:07:31,666
That was decisive!

126
00:07:31,749 --> 00:07:34,919
I've never been very good
at talking to people I don't know.

127
00:07:35,003 --> 00:07:38,923
You really don't have
any interest in romance, huh?

128
00:07:39,507 --> 00:07:41,968
[girl 1] I'm gonna marry teacher
when I grow up!

129
00:07:42,051 --> 00:07:43,303
[girl 2] Me, too!

130
00:07:43,386 --> 00:07:44,762
[Karen] <i>Back in kindergarten,</i>

131
00:07:44,846 --> 00:07:47,849
<i>you were the only one
who was unaffected by Mr. Nakamura.</i>

132
00:07:47,932 --> 00:07:51,561
Everyone was just acting grown-up.
But you may have a point.

133
00:07:51,644 --> 00:07:54,439
I'm not as good
with this stuff as other people.

134
00:07:56,274 --> 00:07:59,736
Could it be, Chii,
that there's someone you like?

135
00:08:03,281 --> 00:08:04,949
[Chinatsu groans]

136
00:08:05,033 --> 00:08:07,702
[Karen] <i>What's up
with this bleak look on her face?</i>

137
00:08:11,331 --> 00:08:13,458
Mm-hm. There is...

138
00:08:14,876 --> 00:08:16,211
<i>someone I like.</i>

139
00:08:17,879 --> 00:08:19,297
[soft music playing]

140
00:08:20,590 --> 00:08:22,550
Is there any chance that it's...

141
00:08:24,427 --> 00:08:25,970
Inomata?

142
00:08:28,431 --> 00:08:29,349
Mm.

143
00:08:31,017 --> 00:08:32,977
So, you're in love with him.

144
00:08:34,812 --> 00:08:36,731
I don't know that I'm there yet!

145
00:08:37,524 --> 00:08:40,568
Huh? You're not sure how you feel?

146
00:08:41,444 --> 00:08:44,822
Hmm... How can I explain it...

147
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,992
Okay, so it's like I'm growing a flower.

148
00:08:48,076 --> 00:08:50,370
[Karen] <i>Here we go again
with her weird metaphors.</i>

149
00:08:50,453 --> 00:08:51,955
When I say that I like him,

150
00:08:52,038 --> 00:08:54,499
I mean that my feelings
have only started to sprout.

151
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:57,502
{\an8}When I'd see him at morning practice,

152
00:08:57,585 --> 00:09:00,713
<i>I just thought of him
as the guy who was always there.</i>

153
00:09:01,673 --> 00:09:05,134
<i>But once I started talking to him,
and got to know him better,</i>

154
00:09:06,135 --> 00:09:10,515
<i>I started feeling attracted to him,
and the sprout began to grow.</i>

155
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:16,271
<i>The more I catch myself
being attracted to him...</i>

156
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:24,904
<i>the bigger the seedling gets.</i>

157
00:09:27,615 --> 00:09:28,533
But then I go...

158
00:09:29,659 --> 00:09:33,538
<i>get tied up playing basketball,
or life gets in the way.</i>

159
00:09:34,372 --> 00:09:37,292
So the flower hasn't had
a chance to blossom yet.

160
00:09:37,375 --> 00:09:39,794
<i>So "blossoming" would be falling in love.</i>

161
00:09:39,877 --> 00:09:43,548
{\an8}On top of that, there was what happened
during the play the other day.

162
00:09:51,431 --> 00:09:54,434
{\an8}I don't know, it took me by surprise.

163
00:09:58,021 --> 00:10:02,275
Well, listen, I'm not the kind of person
who falls in love easily, either.

164
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,694
So I understand how you feel.

165
00:10:04,777 --> 00:10:07,447
{\an8}But all this buzz
about whether they kissed or not...

166
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:09,616
{\an8}It was an accident, so it doesn't matter.

167
00:10:09,699 --> 00:10:12,744
{\an8}I would be out the minute
rumors started spreading around.

168
00:10:12,827 --> 00:10:15,455
{\an8}I would've snapped the seedling off
if I were you.

169
00:10:16,831 --> 00:10:19,459
But I think if you'd ask other people...

170
00:10:20,835 --> 00:10:24,255
some would describe your
"sprouting" feelings as "falling in love."

171
00:10:24,339 --> 00:10:25,965
But that's because everyone's different,

172
00:10:26,049 --> 00:10:29,218
not because there's one correct answer
when it comes to love.

173
00:10:29,302 --> 00:10:33,348
Honestly, with romance,
everyone goes at their own speed.

174
00:10:35,516 --> 00:10:37,018
You aren't the type of person

175
00:10:37,101 --> 00:10:39,937
to go and date someone
just because you want a boyfriend,

176
00:10:40,021 --> 00:10:43,983
and I think that you tend to tread
very cautiously when it comes to dating.

177
00:10:45,610 --> 00:10:47,195
So I guess I understand

178
00:10:47,278 --> 00:10:50,740
why you might not be totally sure
that you're in love with Inomata.

179
00:10:52,742 --> 00:10:53,993
[Chinatsu sighs]

180
00:10:54,077 --> 00:10:57,288
But while you're busy
thinking about it this way,

181
00:10:57,372 --> 00:11:00,249
someone else may come along
and snatch him away from you.

182
00:11:00,333 --> 00:11:02,502
You don't have to be mean like that.

183
00:11:03,086 --> 00:11:04,837
It's just how things work.

184
00:11:05,630 --> 00:11:08,508
Look, all that I'm trying
to get across to you, Chii...

185
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:12,011
is that I want you to have
a great love story of your own.

186
00:11:12,095 --> 00:11:13,012
[Chinatsu exclaims]

187
00:11:13,721 --> 00:11:16,140
[Karen] There's no predicting
when it'll happen.

188
00:11:16,891 --> 00:11:20,770
But when the time comes,
and you realize you do love someone...

189
00:11:21,687 --> 00:11:25,566
I want to make sure
that you accept your own feelings.

190
00:11:28,194 --> 00:11:29,278
{\an8}[Chinatsu] Mm.

191
00:11:30,113 --> 00:11:32,990
[Karen] <i>There are some people
who would say she's already in love.</i>

192
00:11:33,074 --> 00:11:34,534
<i>But if I had to guess...</i>

193
00:11:35,159 --> 00:11:39,080
<i>Chinatsu probably feels like
she's missing one last piece.</i>

194
00:11:42,583 --> 00:11:46,421
My younger sister could stand to learn
a thing or two from you.

195
00:11:46,504 --> 00:11:47,797
Why's that?

196
00:11:48,589 --> 00:11:50,800
She changes her boyfriends like underwear.

197
00:11:51,384 --> 00:11:55,388
Once, she told me she broke up
with someone 'cause he walked too fast--

198
00:11:55,471 --> 00:11:56,556
[Ayame] Sissy!

199
00:11:57,223 --> 00:11:59,183
I need your nail polish remover.

200
00:11:59,267 --> 00:12:01,060
[Karen] Speak of the devil.

201
00:12:01,811 --> 00:12:04,063
I gave it to you the other day, Ayame.

202
00:12:04,147 --> 00:12:05,481
What?

203
00:12:05,565 --> 00:12:07,567
No, you did not. [gasps]

204
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:09,444
Oh! Hi!

205
00:12:09,527 --> 00:12:10,570
Chii!

206
00:12:11,154 --> 00:12:14,824
Your hair's silky as always.
And you have such beautiful skin!

207
00:12:15,450 --> 00:12:17,118
Must be how active you are!

208
00:12:17,201 --> 00:12:19,245
But you hate exercise, right?

209
00:12:19,328 --> 00:12:21,330
What I hate is getting all sweaty.

210
00:12:21,956 --> 00:12:23,249
By the way, Ayame,

211
00:12:23,332 --> 00:12:25,751
didn't you have a date
with your boyfriend today?

212
00:12:25,835 --> 00:12:27,003
I broke up with him.

213
00:12:27,086 --> 00:12:28,087
What, again?

214
00:12:28,171 --> 00:12:29,630
Yeah, again.

215
00:12:29,714 --> 00:12:33,509
Whenever we went to a café,
they'd always ask him to repeat his order!

216
00:12:33,593 --> 00:12:35,845
Like, get it together, and enunciate!

217
00:12:36,804 --> 00:12:38,347
{\an8}But who cares about him!

218
00:12:38,431 --> 00:12:40,600
{\an8}I've already moved on to my next crush.

219
00:12:40,683 --> 00:12:42,435
[Chinatsu gasps]

220
00:12:42,518 --> 00:12:45,354
Chii, you mustn't live by her example.

221
00:12:45,438 --> 00:12:47,231
[Ayame] What are you talking about?

222
00:12:47,315 --> 00:12:50,401
[Karen] About how you completely
have your head in the clouds.

223
00:12:50,485 --> 00:12:53,154
[Chinatsu] What was it that
got you interested in him?

224
00:12:53,237 --> 00:12:54,989
[Ayame] What? Oh, he's hot.

225
00:13:01,329 --> 00:13:02,413
INOMATA

226
00:13:02,497 --> 00:13:03,998
[door sliding]

227
00:13:04,624 --> 00:13:07,001
Thank you again for taking me in.

228
00:13:07,752 --> 00:13:09,754
{\an8}[all] Welcome back, Chinatsu!

229
00:13:10,338 --> 00:13:12,381
{\an8}[Yukiko] Oh, I really missed you!

230
00:13:12,465 --> 00:13:14,800
{\an8}At this point,
it's like you're my own child!

231
00:13:14,884 --> 00:13:16,969
{\an8}[Taiki's grandfather]
Well, come on in, come on in.

232
00:13:17,053 --> 00:13:19,013
{\an8}We'll go and get the rest of your things.

233
00:13:19,639 --> 00:13:22,767
Why don't we have sushi
like the first day she was here?

234
00:13:24,602 --> 00:13:26,020
[grunts softly]

235
00:13:26,103 --> 00:13:27,146
[sighs]

236
00:13:28,105 --> 00:13:31,025
Make way. Cargo is coming through!

237
00:13:31,108 --> 00:13:32,401
I'll take it up.

238
00:13:32,485 --> 00:13:33,694
[Yukiko] You will?

239
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:37,073
[Taiki] <i>As usual,</i>

240
00:13:37,156 --> 00:13:39,784
<i>I can't really tell
what's going through her head.</i>

241
00:13:40,409 --> 00:13:43,204
[sighs softly]

242
00:13:51,295 --> 00:13:52,463
[Hina] Taiki.

243
00:13:53,381 --> 00:13:57,051
I've got a club budget form.
An upperclassman said you needed one.

244
00:13:57,677 --> 00:13:58,594
Thanks.

245
00:13:58,678 --> 00:14:00,388
What happened, did your net snap?

246
00:14:00,471 --> 00:14:01,556
"Strings" not "net."

247
00:14:01,639 --> 00:14:02,598
Yeesh.

248
00:14:02,682 --> 00:14:04,850
You enjoy people's mistakes, huh?

249
00:14:04,934 --> 00:14:06,394
To think you're such a butthead.

250
00:14:06,477 --> 00:14:08,062
I wasn't making fun of you!

251
00:14:08,145 --> 00:14:09,772
Don't you see how they act together?

252
00:14:09,855 --> 00:14:12,066
It seems like
the rumors are true after all.

253
00:14:12,149 --> 00:14:13,359
[girl] No way.

254
00:14:13,901 --> 00:14:15,069
[Taiki grunts]

255
00:14:15,653 --> 00:14:17,655
Don't let it get under your skin.

256
00:14:18,948 --> 00:14:22,577
For my part, I've figured out how to use
those rumors to my advantage.

257
00:14:23,578 --> 00:14:24,579
{\an8}Use them?

258
00:14:24,662 --> 00:14:26,080
"Oh, it's up to Taiki."

259
00:14:26,163 --> 00:14:28,833
"He can make the rumors
real any time he likes."

260
00:14:28,916 --> 00:14:29,834
{\an8}What?

261
00:14:30,459 --> 00:14:31,878
{\an8}O-ho, it's working!

262
00:14:31,961 --> 00:14:33,296
{\an8}[laughs]

263
00:14:33,379 --> 00:14:35,339
{\an8}The groundwork's all but been laid!

264
00:14:35,923 --> 00:14:38,384
I'll stick with this strategy
for the time being!

265
00:14:38,968 --> 00:14:41,137
[Taiki] <i>I was worrying over nothing.</i>

266
00:14:42,221 --> 00:14:43,472
[sighs]

267
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:47,435
<i>Well, I guess that's her own way
of being considerate.</i>

268
00:14:48,185 --> 00:14:49,770
[Kyo] Hmm.

269
00:14:50,646 --> 00:14:52,023
{\an8}[Taiki] Don't even start.

270
00:14:52,106 --> 00:14:53,441
{\an8}I wasn't gonna.

271
00:14:54,942 --> 00:14:56,360
[Coach Yuasa] Everybody, gather up!

272
00:14:56,444 --> 00:14:57,862
[boys] Okay!

273
00:14:57,945 --> 00:14:59,405
[footsteps]

274
00:15:00,197 --> 00:15:04,452
So, I believe I had each of you write down
your goals at the start of the term.

275
00:15:04,535 --> 00:15:07,622
[Taiki] <i>There are a lot of things
I need to think about.</i>

276
00:15:07,705 --> 00:15:10,625
- [Coach Yuasa continues indistinctly]
<i>- But now that the festival's over,</i>

277
00:15:10,708 --> 00:15:13,127
<i>I need to give my full focus
back to practice.</i>

278
00:15:13,753 --> 00:15:16,631
<i>I have to get good enough
to beat Yusa again.</i>

279
00:15:16,714 --> 00:15:19,675
Moving right along, today,
we have a new member joining.

280
00:15:20,217 --> 00:15:22,637
- Really?
- [all murmuring]

281
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:25,389
[Coach Yuasa] Although,
they won't be joining as a player.

282
00:15:26,432 --> 00:15:27,892
Hi, guys!

283
00:15:29,518 --> 00:15:32,772
I'm Ayame Moriya. I'll be your manager!

284
00:15:37,485 --> 00:15:40,655
I'm Ayame Moriya. I'll be your manager!

285
00:15:40,738 --> 00:15:41,697
- [boys gasp]
- What?

286
00:15:41,781 --> 00:15:43,199
But she's so cute.

287
00:15:43,282 --> 00:15:45,910
Our club finally has a girl manager!

288
00:15:45,993 --> 00:15:47,620
{\an8}- All right!
- This rules!

289
00:15:47,703 --> 00:15:50,915
{\an8}[all cheering]

290
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:54,168
Hey, wait. Where's the guy
with the bowl cut?

291
00:15:54,251 --> 00:15:55,169
[boy 1] Huh?

292
00:15:56,504 --> 00:15:59,173
[Ayame] I saw him in this gym
about two weeks ago.

293
00:15:59,256 --> 00:16:02,176
<i>He's super hot, and exactly my type!</i>

294
00:16:02,259 --> 00:16:04,679
<i>Lean but muscular,
cool vibe, and a bowl cut.</i>

295
00:16:05,638 --> 00:16:08,432
[boy 2] Oh,
maybe she's talking about Yusa?

296
00:16:08,516 --> 00:16:10,893
[boy 3] He's a student over at Sajikawa.

297
00:16:10,977 --> 00:16:13,187
He was only here
to play in a practice match.

298
00:16:13,270 --> 00:16:16,691
What? Oh, then I won't be able
to see him every day?

299
00:16:16,774 --> 00:16:18,776
[boy 2] He doesn't even go here.

300
00:16:18,859 --> 00:16:21,654
[Ayame] So I don't get the chance
to wash his uniform?

301
00:16:21,737 --> 00:16:23,239
[boy 3] That's a little sus.

302
00:16:24,281 --> 00:16:25,825
Okay, well, nice knowing you!

303
00:16:25,908 --> 00:16:27,326
- Bye--
- [Haryu] Not so fast!

304
00:16:28,494 --> 00:16:29,704
Kengo.

305
00:16:30,413 --> 00:16:32,623
It's exactly as Karen said.

306
00:16:32,707 --> 00:16:35,459
She knew something was up
when you wanted to do this.

307
00:16:36,043 --> 00:16:38,713
[crying] What other choice did I have?

308
00:16:38,796 --> 00:16:41,215
He matches my type
in the looks department!

309
00:16:41,298 --> 00:16:44,468
I just wanna see that beautiful face
of his and get all blushy!

310
00:16:45,511 --> 00:16:47,722
[boy] Haryu, do you know her?

311
00:16:47,805 --> 00:16:49,598
[Haryu] Girlfriend's little sis.

312
00:16:49,682 --> 00:16:51,475
[Taiki] <i>Oh, she's Karen's sister!</i>

313
00:16:52,143 --> 00:16:55,521
[boy 1] I bet we'll have practice matches
with them again, though. So...

314
00:16:55,604 --> 00:16:57,940
[boy 3] She'll probably see him
at tournaments.

315
00:16:58,024 --> 00:17:00,776
[boy 1] I mean, yeah, this might be
the best way for her to meet him.

316
00:17:02,361 --> 00:17:04,947
Just kidding. You'll be dealing
with me after all.

317
00:17:05,031 --> 00:17:06,991
[boys] <i>She's a real strategist.</i>

318
00:17:07,616 --> 00:17:08,868
All right then, Taiki.

319
00:17:08,951 --> 00:17:10,745
Show our new manager the ropes.

320
00:17:10,828 --> 00:17:11,954
Yes, sir.

321
00:17:21,130 --> 00:17:22,506
[Taiki] This is the storage room.

322
00:17:23,507 --> 00:17:26,010
This is where you mix up
the sports drinks.

323
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,265
And this right here...

324
00:17:32,850 --> 00:17:34,268
is our locker room.

325
00:17:34,351 --> 00:17:35,895
[groans]

326
00:17:35,978 --> 00:17:38,022
Yeah, I know it's a little messy.

327
00:17:38,105 --> 00:17:39,690
A little?

328
00:17:39,774 --> 00:17:41,650
Does no one clean in here?

329
00:17:41,734 --> 00:17:42,777
It stinks!

330
00:17:43,402 --> 00:17:45,780
I honestly can't believe it.

331
00:17:45,863 --> 00:17:47,364
[groans]

332
00:17:47,448 --> 00:17:50,284
[Taiki] <i>She has no trouble
saying what's on her mind.</i>

333
00:17:51,077 --> 00:17:53,079
<i>Haryu said she's Karen's sister.</i>

334
00:17:53,162 --> 00:17:55,539
<i>She doesn't seem like
a bad person, but uh...</i>

335
00:17:56,665 --> 00:17:58,918
[Ayame gasps, shrieks]

336
00:17:59,001 --> 00:18:01,295
There's a spider! Spider!

337
00:18:01,962 --> 00:18:03,547
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>She's so close to me!</i>

338
00:18:03,631 --> 00:18:04,632
[Ayame grunting]

339
00:18:05,591 --> 00:18:06,550
[grunts]

340
00:18:09,178 --> 00:18:11,806
Oh, Chii!! You have to help me!

341
00:18:11,889 --> 00:18:14,058
[Taiki] <i>She's making it sound
like I did something!</i>

342
00:18:14,141 --> 00:18:17,561
- [crying] There's a spider.
- Inomata, what'd you do?

343
00:18:18,145 --> 00:18:19,480
I didn't do anything!

344
00:18:19,563 --> 00:18:21,065
We just found a spider, and...

345
00:18:22,233 --> 00:18:24,944
[screams] It's coming this way!

346
00:18:25,027 --> 00:18:27,613
- Hurry up and make it go away!
- Don't push me!

347
00:18:27,696 --> 00:18:29,824
- I need a tissue!
- Use your bare hands!

348
00:18:31,408 --> 00:18:32,576
[Chinatsu exclaims softly]

349
00:18:38,415 --> 00:18:40,334
Wow, Chii, my hero!

350
00:18:41,335 --> 00:18:45,756
[Taiki] <i>Huh? I thought that Chinatsu
was afraid of bugs.</i>

351
00:18:47,508 --> 00:18:49,635
[Chinatsu] <i>See, that wasn't so bad.</i>

352
00:18:50,177 --> 00:18:51,595
[Taiki] <i>I guess she got over it.</i>

353
00:18:52,930 --> 00:18:56,600
So, what is it that you're doing
in the boys' badminton locker room?

354
00:18:57,226 --> 00:19:00,104
Somehow or other,
I got roped into being their manager.

355
00:19:00,187 --> 00:19:02,398
[Taiki] <i>Come on! You wanted this job.</i>

356
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:04,483
Their manager?

357
00:19:06,735 --> 00:19:09,196
So this guy's been teaching me
how to do the job.

358
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:10,990
Oh, I'm "this guy"?

359
00:19:11,073 --> 00:19:13,659
Oh, right, you have a name, what was it?

360
00:19:13,742 --> 00:19:15,369
Taiki Inomata.

361
00:19:15,452 --> 00:19:17,454
Yeah. "Inota" then.

362
00:19:17,997 --> 00:19:19,123
Huh?

363
00:19:19,748 --> 00:19:24,044
[Ayame] Come on, Inota! We've gotta grab
some trash bags and clean up this pigsty!

364
00:19:24,128 --> 00:19:26,380
[Taiki] Don't call me like I'm your pet!

365
00:19:26,463 --> 00:19:28,299
[door creaks, closes]

366
00:19:28,924 --> 00:19:30,176
[lock clicks]

367
00:19:32,303 --> 00:19:34,138
Okay, well, see you later, Chii!

368
00:19:34,221 --> 00:19:35,472
[gasps softly]

369
00:19:36,473 --> 00:19:38,976
We're gonna need
some rubber gloves for this.

370
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:46,984
When it comes to romance,
everyone goes at their own speed.

371
00:19:49,403 --> 00:19:51,113
{\an8}[Chinatsu] <i>That's what she meant.</i>

372
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:55,659
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

373
00:19:57,870 --> 00:19:59,663
This is so heavy!

374
00:20:00,956 --> 00:20:02,666
[grunts] I did it!

375
00:20:05,753 --> 00:20:08,631
[Hina] <i>So she's the new badminton manager.</i>

376
00:20:09,298 --> 00:20:11,675
Gosh, it's seriously hot.

377
00:20:13,010 --> 00:20:14,178
[Hina gasps]

378
00:20:17,765 --> 00:20:20,559
How do you athletes handle this heat?

379
00:20:21,852 --> 00:20:23,687
All right! [grunts]

380
00:20:23,771 --> 00:20:25,189
[Hina whimpers]

381
00:20:26,190 --> 00:20:28,108
I'm never gonna win.

382
00:20:28,192 --> 00:20:29,944
[Niina] What? Win what exactly?

383
00:20:30,986 --> 00:20:33,113
[Ayame] Fresh electrolytes, everybody!

384
00:20:33,197 --> 00:20:34,406
[indistinct chatter]

385
00:20:34,490 --> 00:20:35,950
Thank you, Manager!

386
00:20:36,033 --> 00:20:37,952
- Oh, I feel alive again!
- [Ayame sighs]

387
00:20:38,035 --> 00:20:39,912
Inota, what's next?

388
00:20:40,704 --> 00:20:42,456
I'll show you the scorekeeping.

389
00:20:42,539 --> 00:20:44,458
Aah! Yeah, let's see!

390
00:20:44,541 --> 00:20:47,711
Um, listen.
It's a bit awkward to say this...

391
00:20:47,795 --> 00:20:48,837
Oh?

392
00:20:49,505 --> 00:20:51,465
But you tend to get really close to me.

393
00:20:52,132 --> 00:20:54,718
{\an8}I'd feel bad
if it caused rumors about you,

394
00:20:54,802 --> 00:20:56,720
{\an8}so it'd be great
if you could back off a little.

395
00:20:57,888 --> 00:20:58,931
Wait, rumors?

396
00:21:03,102 --> 00:21:06,480
Oh! You're the guy who played
Prince Charming in <i>Snow White,</i> right?

397
00:21:06,563 --> 00:21:07,856
You just got it?

398
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:10,025
My friends were talking about it.

399
00:21:10,109 --> 00:21:12,069
It must be weird hearing what people say.

400
00:21:12,152 --> 00:21:14,238
Like speculating
about if you kissed or not.

401
00:21:15,114 --> 00:21:17,741
Everyone's making
a big deal about some silly kiss.

402
00:21:18,450 --> 00:21:20,411
[Taiki] <i>Some silly... kiss?</i>

403
00:21:20,494 --> 00:21:22,997
Anyway, don't get too worked up about it.

404
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:26,750
Pay attention to the people in your life
who really care about you,

405
00:21:26,834 --> 00:21:28,502
and you can just ignore everybody else.

406
00:21:29,295 --> 00:21:30,379
[Taiki gasps softly]

407
00:21:31,088 --> 00:21:35,676
Well, moving on from that,
I'd appreciate it if you'd scoot a bit.

408
00:21:35,759 --> 00:21:37,011
Oops, my bad!

409
00:21:37,094 --> 00:21:38,470
It's just a habit.

410
00:21:38,554 --> 00:21:41,015
[exclaims, groans]

411
00:21:41,098 --> 00:21:43,017
Spider!

412
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:44,893
[screams] It's a...

413
00:21:44,977 --> 00:21:47,771
- a spider! It's a spider! [screams]
- Hey! What did I just say?

414
00:21:49,356 --> 00:21:50,774
Yeah? I had no idea.

415
00:21:50,858 --> 00:21:52,276
[Taiki gasps]

416
00:21:52,359 --> 00:21:54,194
[Ayame] Inota!
Why aren't you doing anything?

417
00:21:54,278 --> 00:21:58,282
{\an8}- [Chinatsu] Oh! I forgot something!
- [Taiki yells]

418
00:21:58,907 --> 00:22:01,869
This is not what it looks like!

419
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
